The stock firmware holds the QCA8084 in reset for 100 ms and waits
another 100 ms before touching it (QSDK mdio-qca.c qca_phy_gpio_set).
The MDIO core default is a 10 us pulse and no wait.
--- a/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq9574-be7000.dts
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq9574-be7000.dts
@@ -615,6 +615,8 @@
 &mdio {
 	status = "okay";
 	clock-frequency = <6250000>;
 	reset-gpios = <&tlmm 60 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+	reset-delay-us = <100000>;
+	reset-post-delay-us = <100000>;
 
 	qca8k_nsscc: clock-controller@18 {
